.SH "NAME"
pcre2_set_max_pattern_compiled_length \- set the maximum length of a compiled pattern
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

int\fP \f(CBpcre2_set_max_pattern_compiled_length\fP\f(CR(
      pcre2_compile_context *\fP\f(CIccontext\fP\f(CR, PCRE2_SIZE\fP \f(CIlength\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function sets, in a compile context, the maximum size (in bytes) for the
memory needed to hold the compiled version of a pattern that is using this
context. The result is always zero. If a pattern that is passed to
\f(CBpcre2_compile()\fP referencing this context needs more memory, an error is
generated. The default is the largest number that a \f(CRPCRE2_SIZE\fP variable can
hold, which is effectively unlimited.
.sp
The limit excludes the fixed, platform\-dependent compiled\-pattern header, which
is included in the total size returned by \f(CBPCRE2_INFO_SIZE\fP. It is not a
limit on temporary compilation workspace, JIT code, or separate character tables.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.